    "text": "Control grows from head and trunk into arms and hands. Many babies roll, push up on arms, grasp purposefully, and accept weight through legs when held in standing. Signs you may notice: Rolls tummy to back or back to tummy; Pushes up on arms during tummy time; Transfers a toy between hands; Reaches while lying on back or tummy. Things to try: Put toys just out of reach to invite rolling; Give floor time on a firm surface; Offer one toy at midline so both hands can meet."
