    "text": "Finding: Baby sign: the one randomized trial found no language advantage; systematic reviews find claims unsupported and no evidence of harm.\nSources: Kirk, Howlett, Pine & Fletcher (2013), To sign or not to sign?, Child Development 84, 574-590 (RCT, N = 40). Johnston, Durieux-Smith & Bloom (2005), First Language 25, 235-251 (review). Fitzpatrick et al. (2014), First Language (systematic review). Bertussi et al. (2026), First Language (N = 1,348 survey, weak to no effect).\nConfidence: HIGH that the acceleration claim is unsupported. Goodwyn, Acredolo & Brown (2000) did report an advantage, but it was not a randomized design and is the study the commercial claims rest on."
