    "text": "Finding: Attachment is relationship-specific (a baby can differ with each caregiver).\nSources: Madigan et al. (2023), below (no differences in distribution by parent); Dagan et al. (2022), New Directions for Child and Adolescent Development, DOI 10.1002/cad.20450.\nConfidence: HIGH. Taught fully in Lesson 3.2.\n\nFinding: Strange Situation: about 20 minutes, 12 to 18 months, two brief separations and reunions; reunion behavior is key; A, B, C, D patterns.\nSources: Ainsworth et al. (1978); Main & Solomon (1990) for disorganization; van IJzendoorn, Schuengel & Bakermans-Kranenburg (1999), Development and Psychopathology, DOI 10.1017/S0954579499002035.\nConfidence: HIGH.\n\nFinding: Global distribution: 51.6% secure, 14.7% avoidant, 10.2% resistant, 23.5% disorganized; 285 studies, 20,720 dyads; more avoidant and disorganized with sociodemographic risk.\nSources: Madigan et al. (2023), The first 20,000 strange situation procedures: a meta-analytic review, Psychological Bulletin, DOI 10.1037/bul0000388.\nConfidence: HIGH. Note: the disorganized rate is higher than the classic 15% for middle-class samples because the pool includes higher-risk samples."
